& [OfficialVocabularyFinding]
  + official Codex documentation exposes state-root installer credential workload-identity trust-store and logging variable families consumed by the CLI or app-server family
  + CODEX_HOME and CODEX_SQLITE_HOME are the relevant public controls for moving app-server state away from ambient user roots
  + credential workload-identity and trust-store inputs are not admissible to the provider-free schema and initialize-only probe
  + official documentation does not claim that its public list exhausts operating-system dependency or subprocess environment reads

& [PredecessorFinding]
  + official Rust semantics make environment inheritance the default and env_clear the primitive for excluding all inherited values
  + the current Phase3A runner removes eight exact Git override names and fixes four noninteractive or pager names
  + it never calls env_clear so it cannot prove B1's closed nonsecret environment identity
  + this finding does not weaken Phase3A's existing authority because B1 is a distinct host interface and the runner remains unchanged

& [CandidateGrammarFinding]
  + B1 should begin with env_clear use an absolute rehashed executable and compare Windows names case-insensitively
  + only disposable CODEX_HOME and CODEX_SQLITE_HOME roots plus separately proven minimal nonsecret operating-system inputs may be admitted
  + raw admitted values remain private while canonical name and value-digest pairs bind evidence
  + provider credentials workload identity CA overrides proxies PATH shell Git hooks pagers editors replacement objects and network helpers remain denied by default
  + this is a candidate grammar and not runtime proof because neither exact local executable has been selected or launched under it

& [SJSDelta]
  + G03 public Codex vocabulary predecessor inheritance threat and env_clear-first candidate grammar are resolved
  + G03 exact minimal operating-system allowlist selected-binary success refusal behavior and canonical serialization remain open
  + G06 state can be redirected through CODEX_HOME and CODEX_SQLITE_HOME but exact disposable roots lifecycle cleanup recovery and ownership remain open
  + G01 executable selection G02 exact schema G04 sandbox response and enforcement G05 carrier and G07 live evidence remain open

& [ThreatDelta]
  + partial env_remove hardening is explicitly insufficient against unknown ambient variables
  + case variants cannot bypass denial on Windows
  + ambient PATH cannot choose or substitute the executable
  + state-root redirection cannot be mistaken for cleanup proof sandbox enforcement or authentication isolation
  + a name-and-digest record must not leak raw credential or path values through errors logs evidence or protocol payloads

